    Use Node.js version from pom.xml in workflows (#8179)
    
    The Maven build pins the Node.js version it uses for the frontend
    modules in the root pom.xml. The documentation build and the LTI tests
    run npm directly on the runner and use whatever Node.js the runner image
    ships, which changes whenever GitHub moves the image. Install the
    version from pom.xml instead so CI and the Maven build cannot drift
    apart and bumping Node.js stays a single edit.
    
    The extraction lives in a small composite action so other workflows can
    share it.
    
